# Enter the flake's development shell on cd, and leave it on cd out.
#
# `use flake` is direnv's own builtin (2.30+), so nix-direnv is not needed. It
# watches flake.nix and flake.lock, and keeps the shell in a profile under
# .direnv/, which doubles as a garbage-collection root — `nix store gc` will
# not delete the toolchain out from under an active checkout.
#
# Optional: nothing in the repository requires direnv. Without it, `nix develop`
# gives the same shell, and a rustup checkout needs neither.
use flake
